<%# the status code, and, above it, the one word this line ever is — tracked out, never stretched, to span
exactly as wide as the number's own first digit does: #error_label_frame is sized in ch at the number's own
font, 1ch being the width a digit glyph is defined by in any font whose figures are tabular, as this one's
are, so it comes out the same whether the first digit actually shown is a wide one or a narrow one %>
<div id="error_code_frame">
	<div id="error_label_frame">
		<div id="error_label">error</div>
	</div>
	<span id="error_code"><%= @status %></span>
</div>

